        "Comparative Anatomy of Vertebrate Alimentary Canals: Modifications of the gut reflecting dietary adaptations: Short, straight intestine in carnivorous sharks equipped with internal spiral valve (typhlosole) to retard transit; Vastly elongated coiled intestines in herbivorous mammals to accommodate microbial fermentation; Gizzard (muscular ventriculus) with ingested grit for mechanical food grinding in birds.",
